## Glycerol
component-glycerol = Glycerol
    .genitive = glycerol
component-glycerol-description-novice = A thick, sweetish, colourless liquid. It mixes with water in any proportion. Added to creams, soap and soap bubbles — so they last longer.
component-glycerol-description-school = Glycerol is about 1400 times more viscous than water. Its specific heat is half that of water, and it boils only at 290 °C.
component-glycerol-model-notes = In reality glycerol supercools easily and often turns glassy instead of crystallising below 17.8 °C. In the model it solidifies at its melting point.
component-glycerol-model-notes-2 = Near its boiling point glycerol starts to decompose; evaporation below boiling is not modelled.
